# Remember things when the power goes off
# Level 5 - Advanced
#
# A brightness setting and a counter of how often the board has started, both kept through power cuts.
# You learn: 'saved var' (kept in EEPROM or flash for you) and resetting it with a long press.
# You need: an LED on pin 9 (with a 220 ohm resistor) and a pushbutton between pin 2 and GND.

board uno

lamp   = pin 9 as pwm
button = pin 2 as input pullup

saved var brightness = 50 %        # loaded at start, saved by itself when it changes
saved var starts = 0

at start:
    starts += 1
    print "Started {starts} times; brightness {brightness}"
    lamp.write(brightness)

on button.clicked:
    brightness += 25 %
    if brightness > 100 %:
        brightness = 25 %
    lamp.write(brightness)
    print "Brightness {brightness} (remembered)"

on button.held(3 s):               # back to the factory settings
    brightness = 50 %
    starts = 0
    lamp.write(brightness)
    print "Settings reset"
